{"id":"west-highland-way","title":"West Highland Way","who":"Classic route · Scotland's best-known long walk","when":"Best May–September (midges from June)","vehicle":"On foot, 5–8 days","kind":"walk","color":"#4338ca","summary":"About 154 km from the edge of Glasgow to Fort William at the foot of Ben Nevis: the bonnie banks of Loch Lomond, old drove and military roads, the empty moor of Rannoch and the Devil's Staircase into Glen Coe country. Inns, bunkhouses and wild camping all the way.","sources":[{"label":"Jodi Bez: West Highland Way, July 2025 (Substack)","url":"https://jodibez.substack.com/p/day-5-i-did-it-my-way"},{"label":"Grant's Tracks: day by day","url":"https://grantstracks.com/posts/whw-day1/"}],"approximate":"The usual overnight stops; the line follows paths near the waymarked route.","km":159,"bbox":[-5.1139,55.9412,-4.3176,56.8218],"stops":[{"name":"Milngavie","place":"Milngavie, Scotland","at":[55.9411,-4.3178],"text":"The granite obelisk in the shopping street marks the start.","source":{"label":"Grant's Tracks: Milngavie to Drymen","url":"https://grantstracks.com/posts/whw-day1/"}},{"name":"Drymen","place":"Drymen, Scotland","at":[56.0655,-4.452],"text":"Farmland and the old railway line to a village with one of Scotland's oldest pubs.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/The_Square%2C_Drymen.jpg/500px-The_Square%2C_Drymen.jpg","page":"Drymen","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Square%2C_Drymen.jpg","credit":"Kenneth Allen","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Rowardennan","place":"Rowardennan, Scotland","at":[56.1514,-4.6414],"text":"Over Conic Hill, the first real climb, with Loch Lomond and its islands below, then along the shore.","source":{"label":"Jodi Bez: Drymen to Rowardennan (2025)","url":"https://jodibez.substack.com/p/a-generally-but-not-all-bad-day-on"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Loch_Lomond_2013_2.JPG/500px-Loch_Lomond_2013_2.JPG","page":"Loch Lomond","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Loch_Lomond_2013_2.JPG","credit":"Mimihitam","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Inverarnan","place":"Inverarnan, Scotland","at":[56.3282,-4.7229],"text":"The rough, rooty northern shore of the loch, then the Drovers Inn, little changed since the cattle drovers.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Drovers_Inn.JPG/500px-Drovers_Inn.JPG","page":"Drovers Inn","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drovers_Inn.JPG","credit":"Smallbones","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Tyndrum","place":"Tyndrum, Scotland","at":[56.4365,-4.7113],"text":"Up Glen Falloch and past Crianlarich to the Highlands proper.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Green_Welly_Stop%2C_Tyndrum_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1498427.jpg/500px-Green_Welly_Stop%2C_Tyndrum_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1498427.jpg","page":"Tyndrum","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_Welly_Stop%2C_Tyndrum_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1498427.jpg","credit":"Oliver Dixon","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Inveroran","place":"Inveroran, Scotland","at":[56.5329,-4.8083],"text":"Under the cone of Beinn Dorain, then over the shoulder to a lonely old inn.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Bridge_of_Orchy-1.jpg/500px-Bridge_of_Orchy-1.jpg","page":"Bridge of Orchy","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bridge_of_Orchy-1.jpg","credit":"Renata (talk)","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Kingshouse","place":"Kingshouse, Glencoe","at":[56.6515,-4.8413],"text":"Across Rannoch Moor on the old military road: wide, wet, wild. Buachaille Etive Mòr stands guard at the end.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Rannoch_Moor.jpg/500px-Rannoch_Moor.jpg","page":"Rannoch Moor","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rannoch_Moor.jpg","credit":"Pip Rolls","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Kinlochleven","place":"Kinlochleven, Scotland","at":[56.7143,-4.9648],"text":"The Devil's Staircase, the highest point of the walk, then a long descent to an old aluminium-smelting village.","source":{"label":"Jodi Bez: day 5 (2025)","url":"https://jodibez.substack.com/p/day-5-i-did-it-my-way"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Kinlochleven.JPG/500px-Kinlochleven.JPG","page":"Kinlochleven","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinlochleven.JPG","credit":"Rmaclean3","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Fort William","place":"Gordon Square, Fort William","at":[56.8164,-5.1139],"text":"Through the Lairigmor and Glen Nevis to the finish in Gordon Square, with Ben Nevis above.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/BenNevis2005.jpg/500px-BenNevis2005.jpg","page":"Ben Nevis","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BenNevis2005.jpg","credit":"Thincat","license":"Public domain"}}],"legs":[{"by":"walk","km":20,"line":[[55.9412,-4.3176],[55.9552,-4.3275],[55.9688,-4.3486],[55.9807,-4.3494],[55.9857,-4.3581],[55.9928,-4.3503],[56.0001,-4.3631],[56.0034,-4.3581],[56.0251,-4.3743],[56.035,-4.3917],[56.0518,-4.4042],[56.0493,-4.4245],[56.0553,-4.434],[56.0652,-4.4385],[56.0655,-4.452]]},{"by":"walk","km":19,"line":[[56.0655,-4.452],[56.0818,-4.5038],[56.0843,-4.5467],[56.0921,-4.5579],[56.0984,-4.5565],[56.1085,-4.5779],[56.1211,-4.5922],[56.1292,-4.6209],[56.1451,-4.6401],[56.1513,-4.6417]]},{"by":"walk","km":34,"line":[[56.1513,-4.6417],[56.1594,-4.6419],[56.168,-4.649],[56.182,-4.6734],[56.1989,-4.6835],[56.2154,-4.674],[56.2421,-4.6844],[56.2443,-4.6726],[56.2507,-4.6672],[56.2492,-4.6373],[56.2551,-4.5847],[56.2627,-4.5797],[56.2798,-4.6021],[56.2965,-4.6472],[56.3241,-4.6895],[56.3318,-4.7208],[56.3283,-4.7231]]},{"by":"walk","km":20,"line":[[56.3283,-4.7231],[56.3304,-4.7161],[56.3419,-4.7138],[56.3573,-4.6739],[56.3683,-4.6578],[56.3816,-4.6481],[56.3896,-4.6326],[56.3945,-4.6504],